# Useful Helpers Workbench - repository ignore rules
#
# Established Tranche 0, 2026-08-05.
#
# This file replaces an inherited copy of the toolkit's own .gitignore, which
# described itself as ignoring "ONLY the toolkit's own output" and was written
# from the toolkit's perspective rather than the repository root's. The
# toolkit keeps its own .gitignore at toolkit/.gitignore; the rules below are
# the workbench root's.
#
# Principle: runtime state and generated artifacts are never checked in, and no
# inherited runtime database, log, or crash record is tracked.

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
.build_venv/

# --- Workbench runtime state (never tracked) ---
# The state root normally resolves to a platform user-data location; a
# development override (USEFUL_HELPERS_STATE_ROOT) may place it here.
/state/
/artifacts/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# --- Toolkit state and exhaust (any depth) ---
# Durable memory is engagement-local; artifacts and exports are regenerable.
_state/
_artifacts/
_exports/
# projectmapper's own output. Regenerable at any time by `projectmapper`.
# Three copies were tracked and 8.4 MB shipped in the payload, carrying
# build-machine absolute paths and filedumped parts-bin content.
_projectmapper/
logs/

# Derived from tools/*/tool.json via `cli registry-refresh`.
toolkit/config/registry.json

# --- Historical harness output ---
# _harness/ is retained as reference evidence; its run output is not.
/_harness/runs/

# --- Installed sidecar copies inside harness targets ---
# The harness copies toolkit/ into <target>/.useful-helpers/ fresh on every run.
# A committed copy is a stale duplicate that drifts from the canonical toolkit:
# one such copy claimed VERSION 1.1.0 while carrying 78 tools against the real 95.
# Never track an installed copy.
_harness/targets/**/.useful-helpers/
**/.useful-helpers/

# --- Gate probes ---
# The gates write a probe file into the repository root to test whether this
# filesystem permits unlink, then delete it. On a filesystem that DENIES unlink -
# the exact condition being probed - the file cannot be removed and lingers. One
# was swept into a commit by `git add -A`. The probe must never be trackable.
.gate-unlink-probe-*
.t01-unlink-probe-*

# --- Test scratch ---
# smoke_test.py and the harness create temporary sidecar installs here.
.useful-helpers-test-tmp/

# --- Removal staging ---
# NOTE: this directory is emptied by the host, so a move here is effectively an
# immediate permanent delete, not reversible staging. Treat it as deletion.
# This sandbox mount denies unlink, so removals are staged here for the operator
# to delete from the host. Never tracked.
/_trash/

# --- Logs and crash records ---
*.log
crash_*.json
crash_*.txt

# --- COMPILED BINARIES AND BUILD OUTPUT (never commit) ---
# A 34 MB NoStringsPDF.exe was tracked; PyInstaller output is regenerable.
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.pyd
*.msi
*.app
**/_Release/
**/_utilities-used-for-installation/

# --- ARCHIVES (never commit) ---
# A 34 MB _NoStringsPDF_backup.tar.gz was tracked - a backup OF the tree it sits in.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz

# --- LARGE DATA, CORPORA AND MODEL BLOBS (never commit) ---
# A 27 MB dictionary corpus was tracked.
*.npy
*.npz
*.bin
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.model
*.pkl
*.parquet
**/_corpuses/
**/corpora/

# --- INHERITED RUNTIME STATE (never commit) ---
# Predecessor apps carry live databases, WAL files, crash dumps and snapshots.
# These are another project's runtime memory, not source.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
**/runtime/snapshots/
**/state/agent_memory*
**/_sandbox/runs/
crash_*/

# --- SECRETS AND SIGNING MATERIAL (never commit) ---
# A code-signing certificate is present in the daily-driver target tree at
# _harness/targets/_UsefulHelperSCRIPTS/_UsefulHelperScriptsMENU/developer_cert.pfx
# and may carry a private key. These patterns are deliberately broad.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.env
*.env
!.env.example
secrets.json
credentials.json
*.credentials

# --- Build output inside reference/target trees ---
/_harness/targets/**/build/
/_harness/targets/**/dist/
*.spec.bak

# --- Editor and OS noise ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Deliberately tracked ---
# .bcc/   builder control: contract, plan, state, provenance, testing, matrix
# _docs/  builder documentation and the active journal
config/registry.json


# --- Test residue written into config/ by smoke runs ---
config/domain-boundary/smoke-*.json
